------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2312.03959] Pop-Stack Operators for Torsion Classes and Cambrian Lattices (https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.03959)\nciteturn9505view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.03959\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 163\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Combinatorics\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 7 Dec 2023]\nL9: # Title:Pop-Stack Operators for Torsion Classes and Cambrian Lattices\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Emily Barnard , cite6†Colin Defant , cite7†Eric J. Hanson L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Pop-Stack Operators for Torsion Classes and Cambrian Lattices, by Emily Barnard and Colin Defant and Eric J. Hanson\nL14: \nL15: cite8†View PDF cite9†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:The pop-stack operator of a finite lattice $L$ is the map $\\mathrm{pop}^{\\downarrow}_L\\colon L\\to L$ that sends each element $x\\in L$ to the meet of $\\{x\\}\\cup\\text{cov}_L(x)$, where $\\text{cov}_L(x)$ is the set of elements covered by $x$ in $L$. We study several properties of the pop-stack operator of $\\mathrm{tors}\\Lambda$, the lattice of torsion classes of a $\\tau$-tilting finite algebra $\\Lambda$ over a field $K$.\nL17: We describe the pop-stack operator in terms of certain mutations of 2-term simple-minded collections. This allows us to describe preimages of a given torsion class under the pop-stack operator.\nL18: > We then specialize our attention to Cambrian lattices of a finite irreducible Coxeter group $W$. Using tools from representation theory, we provide simple Coxeter-theoretic and lattice-theoretic descriptions of the image of the pop-stack operator of a Cambrian lattice (which can be stated without representation theory). When specialized to a bipartite Cambrian lattice of type A, this result settles a conjecture of Choi and Sun. We also settle a related enumerative conjecture of Defant and Williams.\nL19: When $L$ is an arbitrary lattice quotient of the weak order on $W$, we prove that the maximum size of a forward orbit under the pop-stack operator of $L$ is at most the Coxeter number of $W$; when $L$ is a Cambrian lattice, we provide an explicit construction to show that this maximum forward orbit size is actually equal to the Coxeter number.\nL20: Comments:  | 50 pages, 7 figures\nL21: Subjects:  | Combinatorics (math.CO); Representation Theory (math.RT)\nL22: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 05A05, 05A15, 05A19, 05E10, 05E16, 06D75, 06F15, 16G10, 16G20\nL23: Cite as:  | cite10†arXiv:2312.03959 [math.CO]\nL24:    | (or cite11†arXiv:2312.03959v1 [math.CO] for this version)\nL25:    | cite12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2312.03959†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL26: ## Submission history\nL27: \nL28: From: Eric Hanson [cite13†view email ]\nL29: [v1] Thu, 7 Dec 2023 00:22:25 UTC (248 KB)\nL30: \nL31: Full-text links:\nL32: \nL33: ## Access Paper:\nL34: \nL35: View a PDF of the paper titled Pop-Stack Operators for Torsion Classes and Cambrian Lattices, by Emily Barnard and Colin Defant and Eric J. Hanson\nL36: \nL37:   * cite8†View PDF L38:   * cite9†HTML (experimental) L39:   * cite14†TeX Source L40: \nL41: cite15†view license L42: ### Current browse context:\nL43: \nL44: math.CO\nL45: \nL46: cite16†< prev |   cite17†next > L47: \nL48: cite18†new | cite19†recent | cite20†2023-12 L49: \nL50: Change to browse by:\nL51: \nL52: cite21†math L53: cite22†math.RT L54: \nL55: ### References & Citations\nL56: \nL57:   * cite23†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L58:   * cite24†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L59:   * cite25†Semantic Scholar†api.semanti